 "text": "Hi! How are you doing these days? Keep a safe distance, at least few car lengths, so you can stop quickly if one pulls out without a proper signal. Sorry to them, not you. Keep an ear out for signals, and always assume the car is hidden by a bin or tree. Stop completely, never roll on them. Check both ways for traffic, and only proceed when it' clear. I know it is, but it saves accidents. Lots of people just roll without looking, so always assume they will.",
